<title>GERMANY: Bonn mulls sale of D.Telekom by 98-sources.</title>
<headline>Bonn mulls sale of D.Telekom by 98-sources.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government was considering selling 287 million shares in phone company Deutsche Telekom AG this year, coalition sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Bonn was also considering selling its remaining stake in Telekom by the end of 1998 as part of an effort to reduce its budget deficit and qualify for European monetary union (EMU), the sources told Reuters.</p>
</text>
